QtWebEngine's Chromium tree carries a backported PermissionControllerDelegate
whose subscription API is typed, while the Content Shell sources vendored here
still use the untyped int form that was current at the pinned revision:

    ../../content/shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.h:45:7: error:
    conflicting return type specified for 'virtual int
    content::ShellPermissionManager::SubscribePermissionStatusChange(...)'
    note: overridden function is 'virtual
    content::PermissionControllerDelegate::SubscriptionId
    content::PermissionControllerDelegate::SubscribePermissionStatusChange(...)'

    ../../content/shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.h:51:8: error:
    'void content::ShellPermissionManager::UnsubscribePermissionStatusChange(int)'
    marked 'override', but does not override

    ../../content/shell/browser/shell_browser_context.cc:223:58: error: invalid
    new-expression of abstract class type 'content::ShellPermissionManager'

Verified against upstream: at the pinned revision (and as late as 89) both
content/public/browser/permission_controller_delegate.h and
content/shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.* use plain int, so the vendored
Shell sources are internally consistent with the revision they came from. The
tree they are compiled against is not: QtWebEngine's
permission_controller_delegate.h declares
`using SubscriptionId = util::IdType64<PermissionControllerDelegate>` and
returns it, matching what upstream only adopted around 95.

So this is not a vendoring mistake and not a Haiku-specific problem -- it is a
version skew between the pinned Content Shell sources and QtWebEngine's
partially-newer content/public. Fixed by moving the Shell implementation
forward to the typed API, exactly as upstream 95 writes it (SubscriptionId
return type, `return SubscriptionId();`).

Note the two other `PermissionController::kNoPendingOperation` returns in this
file, in RequestPermission and RequestPermissions, are deliberately left alone:
both of those still return plain int in the tree's own
permission_controller_delegate.h, and upstream 95 likewise leaves them as
kNoPendingOperation. Only the subscription pair changed type.

--- a/upstream/content_shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.h
+++ b/upstream/content_shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.h
@@ -42,13 +42,13 @@
       content::PermissionType permission,
       content::RenderFrameHost* render_frame_host,
       const GURL& requesting_origin) override;
-  int SubscribePermissionStatusChange(
+  SubscriptionId SubscribePermissionStatusChange(
       PermissionType permission,
       RenderFrameHost* render_frame_host,
       const GURL& requesting_origin,
       base::RepeatingCallback<void(blink::mojom::PermissionStatus)> callback)
       override;
-  void UnsubscribePermissionStatusChange(int subscription_id) override;
+  void UnsubscribePermissionStatusChange(SubscriptionId subscription_id) override;
 
  private:
   DISALLOW_COPY_AND_ASSIGN(ShellPermissionManager);
--- a/upstream/content_shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.cc
+++ b/upstream/content_shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.cc
@@ -134,16 +134,17 @@
           .GetOrigin());
 }
 
-int ShellPermissionManager::SubscribePermissionStatusChange(
+ShellPermissionManager::SubscriptionId
+ShellPermissionManager::SubscribePermissionStatusChange(
     PermissionType permission,
     RenderFrameHost* render_frame_host,
     const GURL& requesting_origin,
     base::RepeatingCallback<void(blink::mojom::PermissionStatus)> callback) {
-  return PermissionController::kNoPendingOperation;
+  return SubscriptionId();
 }
 
 void ShellPermissionManager::UnsubscribePermissionStatusChange(
-    int subscription_id) {
+    SubscriptionId subscription_id) {
 }
 
